From af49ca0090a92bc8d09e5f282478bea22ebe08e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:14:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: codecs: wcd934x: fix the ADC MUX8 register field

ADC MUX8 sits in bits 5:4 of CDC_TX_INP_MUX_ADC_MUX0_CFG1 (the vendor
tavil driver declares tx_adc_mux8 there), but the enum points at the
same bits of ADC_MUX1_CFG1, the field of ADC MUX10. Two things go wrong:
the "ADC MUX8" control never reaches its own field, and
wcd934x_codec_set_tx_mux() finds no case for (ADC_MUX1_CFG1, shift 4),
so bit 7 of CDC_TX8_TX_PATH_CFG0 (AMIC/DMIC select) is never set and
DEC8 decimates a digital microphone in AMIC mode.

On the Surface Duo the same digital microphone recorded through DEC7 and
DEC8 at once (correlation 0.99) came out 22.5 dB lower on DEC8 at equal
DEC volume.

Point the enum at ADC_MUX0_CFG1 bits 5:4, which wcd934x_codec_set_tx_mux()
already maps to CDC_TX8_TX_PATH_CFG0.
---
 sound/soc/codecs/wcd934x.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd934x.c b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd934x.c
index 3fe277a25..36fa2a6ba 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd934x.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd934x.c
@@ -1034,7 +1034,7 @@ static const struct soc_enum tx_adc_mux7_enum =
 	SOC_ENUM_SINGLE(WCD934X_CDC_TX_INP_MUX_ADC_MUX3_CFG1, 2,
 			ARRAY_SIZE(adc_mux_text), adc_mux_text);
 static const struct soc_enum tx_adc_mux8_enum =
-	SOC_ENUM_SINGLE(WCD934X_CDC_TX_INP_MUX_ADC_MUX1_CFG1, 4,
+	SOC_ENUM_SINGLE(WCD934X_CDC_TX_INP_MUX_ADC_MUX0_CFG1, 4,
 			ARRAY_SIZE(adc_mux_text), adc_mux_text);
 
 static const struct soc_enum rx_int0_1_interp_mux_enum =
-- 
